    "body": "Adds ADR-012, which decides how the browser handles standard CSS box-model shorthands.\n\n## The bug this fixes\n\nToday `p { margin: 10px 20px }` silently vanishes: `Stylesheet::parse` stores the raw multi-value string, `parse_px` rejects it, layout sees `0`. The same happens with `margin-top: 10px` written directly, because `fill_sides` reads only the shorthand name.\n\nEvery contributor who writes normal CSS hits this and sees a browser that \"doesn't do margins.\"\n\n## The decision\n\nTwo coordinated changes:\n\n1. **Parse-time expansion.** `Stylesheet::parse` expands `margin`, `padding`, and `border-width` in 1/2/3/4-value form into four longhand declarations each, before cascade sees them.\n2. **Longhand consumption in layout.** `fill_sides` reads `margin-top`/`margin-right`/`margin-bottom`/`margin-left` (and the padding/border equivalents) individually.\n\nThe cascade and paint layers are untouched. `Declaration`, `Rule`, `Stylesheet`, `ComputedStyle`, and `LayoutBox` are all unchanged.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Shorthands: `margin`, `padding`, `border-width`\n- Value forms: 1, 2, 3, or 4 space-separated values (CSS 2.1 section 8.1)\n\n## Deferred\n\n- `border` shorthand, `border-color` (requires `LayoutBox` struct change)\n- `background`, `font`, `overflow`, `list-style` shorthands\n- `calc()`, `var()`, CSS-wide keywords (`inherit`, `initial`, `unset`)\n- `auto` margins (requires container-aware centering)\n- Named border widths (`thin`, `medium`, `thick`)\n\n## Diagrams\n\nADR-012 includes three ASCII diagrams, following the convention established in ADR-011:\n\n1. The four-value clock (top, right, bottom, left order)\n2. The 1/2/3/4-value expansion table\n3. The per-value layout effect\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `src/renderer/css/stylesheet.cpp` — `expand_shorthand` helper, called from `add_declaration`\n- `src/renderer/layout/layout.cpp` — `fill_sides` reads longhand properties\n- `tests/test_stylesheet.cpp` — ~10 expansion tests\n- `tests/test_layout.cpp` — ~4 longhand consumption tests\n\nNo new files. No CMake changes.\n\n## Next\n\nOnce ADR-012 merges, the implementation issue will be \"Implement shorthand expansion per ADR-012\" — two commits (parse-time expansion, then layout longhand consumption), same rhythm as #109.\n",
